{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"A\": \"Research order-preserving search-space pruning. Replace flat enumeration with recursive Heap traversal proven equivalent to the supplied iterative order. Within a block permuting positions [0,k), the suffix is fixed: prune when its mapped vertices violate loop/degree compatibility or adjacency, or when remaining vertices have no feasible assignments consistent with that suffix. Use only necessary conditions. Crucially, precompute each block's exact endpoint permutation and apply it when skipping the block, so subsequent traversal remains unchanged. Avoid factorial-sized counters or ranks that overflow for n<100. Preserve the initial identity shortcut and otherwise emit every successful mapping in reference order. Deliver a complete independently measured candidate; prioritize cheap pruning before expensive domain checks.\",\n  \"B\": \"Research low-overhead verification and output without changing Heap enumeration. Replace vector<vector<bool>> proxy accesses with compact contiguous adjacency storage, preserving diagonal entries. Cache a counterexample vertex pair: recheck it first for each candidate, reject immediately if it still mismatches, and otherwise run an exact short-circuit scan that records a new witness. A cached pair must never establish acceptance. Benchmark against ordinary early-exit scanning; maintaining every mismatch after every swap may cost more than it saves. Buffer output in bounded chunks rather than flushing with endl, retaining identical integer formatting, trailing spaces, line order and newlines. Keep startup and allocation overhead low. Deliver a complete measured candidate with verification and buffering improvements separable.\",\n  \"C\": \"Research structural rejection and candidate filtering. Keep size checking and the successful identity path cheap. Derive invariants from the actual Boolean adjacency matrix, not declared edge counts: loop flags, off-diagonal degrees, component signatures, then jointly computed color refinement using exact signatures and shared color identifiers across both graphs. Unequal corresponding signature/color multiplicities prove non-isomorphism; equal colors never prove isomorphism. During unchanged Heap enumeration, maintain the number of vertex mappings incompatible with the final colors, updating the two swapped positions in constant time; verify adjacency only when this count is zero. Stage preprocessing and measure whether deeper refinement repays its overhead. Deliver a standalone candidate and expose compatibility information for A's block pruning.\",\n  \"G\": \"Integrate programs actually produced by A/B/C, starting from the best independently measured candidate. Add compatible changes incrementally and retain the fastest validated standalone or combination; gains are not assumed additive. In particular, skipped Heap blocks must leave the permutation, color counters and any verification metadata consistent; cached witnesses should be rechecked against the resulting mapping. Audit identity-only output, nonidentity multiple-match ordering, no-match output, unequal sizes, self-loops and duplicate-edge collapse. Validate and time through the unchanged evaluator within existing budgets, considering the baseline's millisecond-scale variation. Prefer portable, low-overhead CPU implementations over unmeasured threading. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, target, permissions or budgets, and never specialize to measured inputs or expected answers.\",\n  \"analysis\": \"Only Problem A's src/brute_isomorphism.cpp is the optimization target. The valid baseline averages 9.586 ms, with samples 9.438–9.773 ms and four correctness cases; there is no profile or workload-size evidence. The target is four-core ARM64 without GPUs. The key correctness trap is that the source differs from the statement's single-mapping description: a successful identity check prints only identity and returns, but otherwise Heap enumeration continues and prints every successful permutation in order. Preserve that observable behavior, including trailing spaces and the no-isomorphism message. Adjacency is undirected Boolean storage: self-loops matter and repeated edges collapse. The three research directions separate search pruning, verification/output costs, and structural filtering; integration must be measured rather than presumed beneficial.\"\n}"}}
